# The family's baseline block, byte-identical in every checkout that carries it,
# so what a routine editable install or test run drops is ignored in the repo
# that drops it. The eleven files were written independently and covered
# different subsets of the same artifacts, which left several trees dirty after
# a plain `pip install -e .` -- and a dirty tree here blocks every agent's merge.
# This repo's own entries go under the marker below, never in here.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tmp-pytest-*/

# Windows shortcuts are machine-specific and embed the real install path.
*.lnk

# pCloud conflict copies (this dir syncs via pCloud). Never our files; an
# untracked one dirties main and blocks merges. '[' escaped to match literally.
*\[conflicted*

# --- evolver's own ---

# The app's own logs, at the root where it writes them.
*.log

# A virtual environment under the other name people give one.
venv/

# The type checker's cache, which only this repo runs.
.mypy_cache/

# The prompt-scrape browser profile now lives in the system temp dir; the glob
# stays to cover a leftover copy in a checkout that ran the older code.
.tmp-prompt-browser-profile/

# Non-AI upscale runtime state now lives under LOCALAPPDATA\Evolver; the globs
# also cover leftover copies in the repo root, including the "[conflicted N]"
# duplicates the file sync service used to make of the old in-repo state files.
nonai_upscale_job*.json
nonai_upscale_attempts*.json
nonai_upscale_cooldown*.json
.nonai-upscale-skip*.txt
.nonai-upscale-next*.txt
# The pin manifest is rewritten whole, through a temp file beside it.
.nonai-upscale-next*.tmp

# Left by a regeneration mode this app no longer has -- no code has referenced
# either name since March. Both files are still in this checkout, so un-ignoring
# them would leave the tree permanently dirty, which is the failure the block
# above exists to prevent; they go when the files do.
.regen-skip.txt
.regen-complete

# GUI runtime state
runs/
# The branch preview's own tree: the launcher's log lands there.
state/
gui_settings.json

# Private overlays — real values live here and never get published. Each has a
# committed *.example.* template that documents its shape.
#   real copy — spoken act vocabulary and provider details
/content.local.json
